<%- include('partials/mkt_header', {
  title: "Membership Terms — Uma's Books and Adventures",
  description: "Terms of membership at Uma's Books & Adventures.",
}) %>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <span class="kicker" data-i18n="mt.kicker">Legal</span>
    <h1 data-i18n="mt.title">Membership Terms</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="muted small" data-i18n="mt.updated">Last updated: October 2026.</p>

      <p data-i18n="mt.intro">These are the terms of membership at Uma’s Books &amp; Adventures, a non-profit association in Albi, France. By registering for membership, you agree to them.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s1.h">What membership is</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s1.p">Membership is a contribution to our non-profit association — the shop, our English programs, and community events — and gives you a say in how part of what we raise is used. It is not a purchase of goods or a subscription service. The amount is the one shown on the HelloAsso membership form when you join.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s2.h">Benefits</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s2.p">Members can vote on the charity our association supports each quarter, join the members' discussion forum, and get access to special events, engagements, and a member tote bag. We may add, change, or retire specific benefits from time to time as the association's activities evolve — see the Membership page for the current list.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s3.h">Joining and payment</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s3.p">Membership is linked to an account on this site. If you do not have one, the Membership page creates it for you in the same step (your name and email), then you pay online through HelloAsso, our secure payment provider, using the form on that page; we never see or store your card details. We email you a link: after paying, click it to confirm your address and choose your password. If you already have an account, log in first and pay from the Membership page. There is no manual review. Once your email is confirmed and the payment has gone through, your membership is attached to your account automatically. To make this work, pay with the same email address as your account on this site, and make sure that email address is confirmed; a payment made with a different email, or matching an account whose email is not verified, cannot be matched automatically — in that case write to admin@umasbooks.org and we will sort it out.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.sd.h">Duration and expiry</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.sd.p">Membership lasts 12 months from the date of your payment. It is not renewed automatically: when the 12 months are over your membership ends and your member benefits stop (your account stays open). To continue, join again through the same form with the same email address; the new payment then runs for 12 months from its own date.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s4.h">Community conduct</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s4.p">The discussion forum and community spaces are here to connect people over books and shared interests. We ask that members treat each other with respect — no harassment, hate speech, spam, or illegal content. We may remove content or suspend a member's access for violating this, particularly where it affects other members' or volunteers' safety or wellbeing.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s5.h">Ending your membership</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s5.p">You can ask us to close your membership and account at any time by emailing admin@umasbooks.org. Your contribution supports activities already under way, so it is not refundable, except where required by law or if your payment is refunded to you (for example, a payment made in error or a payment dispute upheld by HelloAsso); in that case the membership it paid for ends.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s6.h">Your data</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="mt.s6.p">When you join, HelloAsso collects the details you enter on its form. We keep the email you paid with, the amount and the date of your payment, so that we can activate your membership and know when it ends. See our <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle this information.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s7.h">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p data-i18n="mt.s7.p">If we make significant changes to these terms, we'll update the date at the top of this page and, where practical, let current members know.</p>

      <h2 data-i18n="mt.s8.h">Contact</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="mt.s8.p">Questions about membership: <a href="mailto:admin@umasbooks.org">admin@umasbooks.org</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
